# Lagari — Project intelligence for Cursor

## Session start

1. Read ALL files under `memory-bank/` before substantive work.
2. Read `docs/plan/PLATFORM-PLAN.md` and `docs/plan/ROADMAP.md` for current phase and decisions.
3. For Next.js code in `lagari-fe/`, read and follow `lagari-fe/AGENTS.md`.
4. Before using Next.js APIs, check `lagari-fe/node_modules/next/dist/docs/` for current behavior and deprecations.

## Frontend package

- Path: `lagari-fe/`
- Stack: Next.js 16, React 19, Tailwind 4, TypeScript, App Router (`app/`)

## Planning docs (source of truth for new sessions)

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `docs/plan/` | Platform plan, roadmap, session log |
| `docs/adr/` | Architecture decision records |
| `docs/architecture/` | ERD, OpenAPI MVP contract |
| `docs/design/` | Luxury visual direction |
| `docs/requirements/` | FR, NFR, gap matrix, glossary |

## Memory Bank

- Update `memory-bank/activeContext.md` and `memory-bank/progress.md` after significant planning or implementation; user may say **update memory bank**.

## Skills

- Use `@cursor-memory-bank` for memory bank workflow.
- Storefront UX: `@frontend-design`; implementation: `@frontend-developer` (override Next version with `lagari-fe/AGENTS.md`).

## Implementation gate

- **No** `lagari-be` or commerce UI until user approves P1 plan and says **execute** for P2+.
